From a7f26419f5f7aff12b97f5ed89451a81c96d3e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claudeus <claudeus@kub0.ai>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 11:20:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Add sessions rename CLI and hook
 sessionTitle/terminalSequence.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Local fork only — upstream does not accept PRs. grok sessions rename
pins title_is_manual on disk (same storage path as x.ai/session/rename).
Hooks may return Claude-shaped sessionTitle + allowlisted OSC (0/1/2/9/99/777, BEL);
the pager writes the sequence (no /dev/tty). /rename --auto stays unpin.

Rebased onto upstream/main 7581004. HookRunResult::Success gained
session_title/terminal_sequence, so every 4-field construction site now uses
the with_message() ctor — including the PostToolUse sites upstream added since.
HookRunnerResult::Observe joins the Success/Stop catch-all arms alongside
upstream's PostToolUse. protocol.rs gains the std::io::Write import that
emit_raw_sequence needs.

Co-Authored-By: Grokus <grokus@kub0.ai>
Co-Authored-By: Claudeus <claudeus@kub0.ai>
